 "answer": "The limit is **32 TB** per non-partitioned table with the default 8 KB block size. Postgres addresses table data with 32-bit block numbers, so the maximum is 2³² blocks × 8 KB. The number of vectors that fits depends on their size. For example, a 768-dimension float4 vector takes about 3 KB, so billions of rows would fit before reaching the limit. Partitioning is the usual way around this limit.\n\nI don't know of any project-specific setting that changes this, so I'm going by the standard Postgres limit.",
